{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "More funding for research looking into expanded routine screening of newborns",
        "additional_details": "I want to prevent other families experiencing the heartbreak of losing a baby. Current newborn screening detects some serious conditions, but others may go undetected. We believe research is needed to establish whether broader, repeated blood screening could identify life-threatening illnesses and infection earlier, improve treatment and reduce preventable infant deaths, including some sudden unexpected deaths",
        "background": "Increase funding for research into voluntary heel-prick blood screening for all newborns at birth and every two weeks until eight weeks old. The aim is to investigate whether expanded testing could detect life-threatening illnesses/infection earlier to prevent avoidable infant deaths",
